<p>Okay, accidentally posted this early (don't ask how you accidentally post something, I feel really stupid), so I'm writing the author's post now instead of later. Yay! Yay&#8230; Anyways! This came out of Draft Swap, which is a little experiment put on by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/varaxous" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2433554); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2433554&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1548004075" alt="Varaxous" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2433554)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/varaxous" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2433554); return false;">Varaxous</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rimple" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2320004); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2320004&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1548004075" alt="Rimple" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2320004)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rimple" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2320004); return false;">Rimple</a></span> in which people traded drafts that they had lost motivation for to other people. If it goes well, this could become a regular thing (and maybe get its own tag in the future, which would be awesome). I actually got stuck with Rimple's draft, which was just some lines of description and scribbled notes about a call in which someone is attacked by birds wanting money, and another log in which a D-Class enters a Burger King run by crows.</p>
<p>Everything past those key points is conceptualized by yours truly, and Jimminy Christmas it has been fun.</p>
<p>Rimple had a one off line about Wilson's Wildlife Solutions, and then I turned them into a whole GoI with a (what I felt to be) unique relationship with the Foundation, and furthermore a unique approach to anomalies (or unusualities). Special thanks to a whole <em>slew</em> of people who reviewed this, who I actually don't want to mention by name because I <em>will</em> forget some of them&#8230; but I'll do it anyways.</p>
